@startuml
title Tseho Watch GUI state machine v0

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #111111
  BorderColor #DDDDDD
  FontColor #EEEEEE
}
skinparam ArrowColor #DDDDDD
skinparam BackgroundColor #000000

[*] --> Home

state Home {
  [*] --> StrictWatchface
  StrictWatchface : default debug skin
  ColorWatchface : legacy first prototype
  StrictWatchface --> ColorWatchface : toggleSkin
  ColorWatchface --> StrictWatchface : toggleSkin
}

Home --> DeviceList : tap devices
Home --> EventJournal : tap events
Home --> Diagnostic : tap time area

DeviceList --> DeviceOverview : tap device
DeviceOverview --> ParameterList : tap parameters
ParameterList --> MetricDetail : tap metric
DeviceOverview --> ControlList : tap controls
ControlList --> CommandStatus : tap command
ControlList --> CriticalRequest : hold critical action

EventJournal --> EventDetail : tap event
Home --> EventDetail : present blocking event
DeviceList --> EventDetail : present blocking event
DeviceOverview --> EventDetail : present blocking event
ParameterList --> EventDetail : present blocking event
MetricDetail --> EventDetail : present blocking event
ControlList --> EventDetail : present blocking event
CommandStatus --> EventDetail : present blocking event
CriticalRequest --> EventDetail : present blocking event
Diagnostic --> EventDetail : present blocking event

CommandStatus --> CommandStatus : submit / sending
CommandStatus --> CommandStatus : result success
CommandStatus --> CommandStatus : result rejected
CommandStatus --> CommandStatus : result timeout

CriticalRequest --> CriticalRequest : submit / waiting
CriticalRequest --> CriticalRequest : result approved
CriticalRequest --> CriticalRequest : result denied

DeviceList --> Home : back
DeviceOverview --> DeviceList : back
ParameterList --> DeviceOverview : back
MetricDetail --> ParameterList : back
ControlList --> DeviceOverview : back
CommandStatus --> ControlList : back
CriticalRequest --> ControlList : back
EventJournal --> Home : back
EventDetail --> EventJournal : back or ack
Diagnostic --> Home : back

note right of Home
  The default visual variant is the second
  strict/context watchface. The color-context
  prototype remains available through Diagnostic.
end note

note bottom
  Runtime implementation currently lives in watch_ui.c:
  screen enum, small navigation stack, semantic hit targets,
  and lifecycle phases for command/critical flows.
end note
@enduml
